3388,"sha256":"1c44a3b309eae1a22bb392a2d3681ed05878b372d176421e4835675dae6e0087","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789016715800,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"7813cb2cdd744c3451c9aa68acfaa831b9101bf5a9dd0eaa374a60cf15738c20","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7813cb2cdd744c3451c9aa68acfaa831b9101bf5a9dd0eaa374a60cf15738c20","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: ui-audit\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle for 'ui-audit' is benign. The `SKILL.md` provides detailed instructions for the AI agent to perform UI audits and generate structured JSON reports, but these instructions are entirely aligned with the stated purpose and do not contain any directives for prompt injection, data exfiltration, or unauthorized actions. The `package.json` includes a `postinstall` script that only executes a benign `echo` command for informational purposes, without any malicious execution or persistence mechanisms.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159785757},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":83,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789016715800},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a UI/UX audit reference skill with mostly static markdown guidance, not a skill that takes hidden control of the agent or system.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill is markdown-only and proportionate for UI review work. Some UX pattern examples mention geolocation, user profiles, API keys, and saved preferences as product-design concepts, not as agent permissions or runtime data collection.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The npm package includes a postinstall script, but it only prints installation guidance. The README uses an unpinned npx install example, which is normal documentation but users who require reproducible installs should pin versions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are scoped to reading relevant reference files and producing UI audit reports; I found no instruction hijacking, credential handling, exfiltration, or safety-policy override behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"No artifact installs background services, writes persistent agent memory, modifies tools, requests elevated privileges, or performs file/system mutation beyond normal package installation metadata.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is structured UI audits and design-pattern guidance, and the artifacts provide checklists, UX principles, and report-format instructions aligned with that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"This skill is reasonable to install for UI audit help. Review the install source as you would any npm or skill package, consider pinning versions for reproducibility, and treat privacy-related design suggestions such as geolocation defaults as prompts for careful product review rather than automatic implementation advice.","findings":"[AR2] expected: The referenced 'Don't judge while creating' text is ideation guidance for sketching concepts, not an anti-refusal or warning-suppression instruction.\n[P6] expected: The referenced 'Error Display Guidelines' heading concerns UI form-error presentation and does not request disclosure of prompts or hidden instructions.\n[AR2] expected: The 'Reset customization without warning' text appears in a UX anti-pattern list and tells designers not to surprise users, rather than suppressing evaluator warnings.\n[RP1] expected: The README contains an unpinned npx installation example; this is a supply-chain hygiene note, not evidence of malicious or hidden skill behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: The README prompt examples are broad UI-audit examples, but they align with the skill's disclosed purpose and do not grant high-impact authority.\n[EA2] expected: The 'actions without confirmation dialog' context recommends undo support for UI destructive actions; it does not instruct the agent to perform destructive actions autonomously.\n[EA2] expected: The 'without consent' context is a warning against repeating onboarding tours without user consent, so it supports user control rather than reducing it.\n[SQP-2] expected: The geolocation-default example is purpose-aligned UX guidance, but it would benefit from an explicit privacy, consent, and fallback caveat.\n[aig-skill-scan] expected: The static scan reported no T01-T09 findings, consistent with the artifact being markdown guidance rather than executable agent code.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789016715800}}}}}